  "notes": "Cash-basis village. Governmental lines from the governmental funds statement Total column (p4); interest income 54 is printed under Other Financing Sources (Uses) and is recorded in other_financing (as FY2024); transfers out 1,659. Spending is partly by object (Personnel services, Operating expenses, Supplies and materials) with mixed General/Street columns. Governmental cash left null and fund balance used for the roll-forward, as in FY2023/FY2024 (cash printed on p1/p3: 164,880 + county treasurer 1,332 at year end; no beginning cash printed). Business-type from the proprietary funds statement Total column (p6); interest, ARPA grant, lagoon loan receipts, loan payments, interest expense and capital outlay are printed under 'Other receipts (disbursements)' below the total (outside_printed_total). Sewer 'Other' 15,471 counted as charges for services per Statement of Activities (p2). Proprietary cash flow statement (pp7-8) is cash basis; proprietary left null as in later years. Several 1-dollar rounding gaps recorded in report_discrepancies. Balance sheet: governmental from the governmental funds statement of assets and fund balances (p3, totals equal government-wide 166,212), proprietary from the Statement of Net Position (p1). The only supplementary schedule is the all-funds budgetary statement (p9), so detail is per fund column of the governmental and proprietary statements per user rule; p9 not recorded. Read pages 1-9 of 9"
